Sonic The Last Hope for AmigaOS 3 - @RELEASE_VERSION@
==================================================

The Amiga OpenSurge engine, ready to play Sonic The Last Hope,
a fan game made with the Open Surge Engine. No separate engine install is
needed.

THIS ARCHIVE HAS NONE OF THE GAME'S OWN FILES. Its makers have not said
they may be passed on, so they are not. Download the game yourself, from
its page:

  https://sonicfangameshq.com/forums/showcase/sonic-the-last-hope.1543/

  file     Sonic The Last Hope.rar
  size     77299133 bytes
  sha256   eb0daac18a3762218dedad340528fb2ac7cf70548de1ac109bd78dda2d3bd391

The game, its characters and its music belong to their makers and owners;
it is not made by or for SEGA.

Installing
----------
Double-click Install-SonicTLH beside the SonicTLH drawer. It checks the CPU,
FPU and GFOpenGPU, asks where the SonicTLH drawer should go (Work:Games is
offered), copies the engine there, and then asks for the game you
downloaded:

- Sonic The Last Hope.rar is a RAR archive, which AmigaOS cannot unpack by
  itself: unpack it with an UnRAR from Aminet (util/arc) or on another
  computer
  (7-Zip), copy the "Sonic The Last Hope" folder to the Amiga
  and choose that folder;
- or the folder "Sonic The Last Hope" that unpacking it made;
- or a game.zip made from the download on another computer with the port's
  scripts/prepare-amiga-port.sh.

It checks the folder's name and the sizes of a few of its files, then
copies the game's files into SonicTLH/Game, leaving out the Windows program
files. It then updates the menu script for OpenSurge 0.6.1 with
Tools/PatchMenu.rexx (ARexx; RexxMast is started if it is not running) and
adds Tools/surge.cfg. Running Install-SonicTLH again replaces or keeps
those files.

A computer with a shell can check the download's SHA-256 first:
  sha256sum "Sonic The Last Hope.rar"

What is in the drawer
---------------------
StartGame   starts the game (once its files are installed)
Engine/     the OpenSurge engine (below)
Game/       the game's own files, from your download (Install-SonicTLH)
Tools/      what Install-SonicTLH uses
Licences/   licences and the engine's source

What it needs
-------------
- AmigaOS 3.2 (Installer 43.3 or newer for Install-SonicTLH)
- a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU
- GFOpenGPU: LIBS:GFOpenGPU/GL.module and SDL2.module (as on AmiCradle)
- about 300 MB free on the hard disk, and plenty of Fast RAM

The engine
----------
Engine/ is Amiga OpenSurge, Open Surge Engine 0.6.1.3 for AmigaOS 3,
exactly as released:

  release   @ENGINE_REPO@ @ENGINE_TAG@
  commit    @ENGINE_COMMIT@
  archive   @ENGINE_ASSET@
  sha256    @ENGINE_SHA256@
  program   Engine/opensurge
  sha256    @ENGINE_BINARY_SHA256@
  compiler  @ENGINE_COMPILER@

No separate engine install is needed: StartGame runs this copy. The engine
keeps its settings, logfile.txt and the game's compatibility pack in
Engine/ (Engine/.userdata). Licences/SOURCE.txt says where its source is.

Starting and playing
--------------------
Double-click StartGame in the SonicTLH drawer. From a Shell, CD to the
drawer first, then Execute StartGame. F10 switches between a window and
the full screen. Leave the game from its own menu (Esc brings it up in
most games).

